    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of women who attended the party. We can use the given information about the number of men and the number of dances each man and woman participated in.\n\nHere are the steps to solve the problem:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dances each man participated in:**\n   Each man danced with exactly 3 women.\n\n2. **Identify the total number of dances each woman participated in:**\n   Each woman danced with exactly 2 men.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of dances:**\n   Since there are 12 men and each man danced with 3 women, the total number of dances is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women per man} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of dances each woman participated in:**\n   Since there are 12 women and each woman danced with 2 men, the total number of dances is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ women} \\times 2 \\text{ men per woman} = 24 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine the number of women:**\n   Since each dance involves one man and one woman, the total number of dances must equal the total number of dances each man participated in. Therefore, the number of women is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{36 \\text{ dances}}{2 \\text{ dances per woman}} = 18 \\text{ women}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
